# oracle: native binary restart of dihedral multi/harmonic with improper harmonic (dihedral_multi_harmonic.cpp a1..a5); 16 chains of 6 atoms (atom_style full, dihedral.data with bonds, angles, dihedrals and impropers), 50 steps written natively, then read and continued for 100 steps
# oracle-inputs: w185nr_dihedral_multi.restart
# native: b332f28 built as the parity binary wrote w185nr_dihedral_multi.restart (lj/cut or lj/charmm/coul/charmm pair with zero epsilon)
read_restart    w185nr_dihedral_multi.restart
neighbor        0.3 bin
thermo_style    custom step temp epair ebond eangle edihed eimp etotal press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          50
fix             1 all nve
run             100
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-9 abs=1e-12
# measured: max relative error 4.0e-12 (native restart continuation, engine vs native thermo and per-atom), so the tolerance is 1e-9
